+# CineWeave Studio · 黑色纪录片工作台
 
-# Design System: CineWeave Studio Graphite Candidate
+2026-11-09。采用用户已确认的 MOMENTUM 参考方向，接入既有私有 Studio。正式源码基线为 Site v102；本文件描述当前实现，发布与验证结果见 docs/momentum-production-20261108.md。
 
-## Overview
+## 颜色与字体
 
-**Creative North Star: "A projection room opening onto a private creative desk"**
+共享语义变量位于 components/ui/studio-tokens.css，React、Portal 和原生素材页面共用。底色 #080909，内容面 #101211，浮层 #151716，正文 #f2f1eb，次级字 #aaa9a0，分隔 #eeede52e，输入边界 #eeede55c。金色 #c8aa72 只用于主动作、选中与关键状态；焦点 #d9c59d。状态色继续使用语义变量。透明控件以暖白边线建立层次，普通页面不叠加雾化或彩色光晕。
 
-CineWeave uses one graphite, warm cream and copper system across home, working pages, portals and native compatibility controls. The entrance frames the actual selected work with a bounded light field and honestly captioned catalog reference. Fixed interface headings carry a serif voice; user-authored work titles use the UI face. Reading, editing and review use stable surfaces, concise controls and minimal motion within that same palette.
+自托管 CW Sans（Noto Sans SC 子集，100–900）用于中文界面与正文；缺字回退系统中文字体。CW Condensed（Barlow Condensed 700）用于品牌与拉丁展示文字，CW Mono（IBM Plex Mono 400）仅用于数字与代码。public/fonts 保留 SIL OFL 授权、来源及子集元数据。用户内容以可读性优先，正文 14–15px、1.85–1.95 行距，不以装饰字体处理长文。
 
-This records the built Phase42 consistency candidate and Phase43 graph-body rebuild after v49's inconsistent-theme rejection and the owner's rejection of the earlier graph internals. Phase43 introduces compact avatar/name/identity cards, project-role and story-event lanes, direct-relationship focus and an accessible list alternative within the same world. It remains UNAPPROVED, with no approved current image comp or QUALITY BAR artifact. Independent final visual review returned ship; owner graph acceptance remains pending.
+## 页面与交互
 
-Phase42 independent review returned FIX; its F1-F3 fix batch and local checks are historical evidence, with native catalog/admission interpretation and persisted truth under follow-up. Phase43's six recaptured desktop/mobile screenshots are under output/playwright/cw-p43-*.png. Independent final review returned ship after F43-1 full-bounds correction, with no correction regression across those captures. The first detector pass reported five advisories; intentional compact graph support type and semantic dots are scoped below. The final corrected build passed; publication remains pending. This record establishes neither whole-product completion nor owner approval, hosted owner login or physical iOS behavior. Source readiness remains BLOCKED without supplied hosted evidence.
+桌面左侧菜单 200px，较窄桌面 180px，包含看板、项目、演员、素材；连接与更多工具位于底部。767px 以下改为 64px 顶栏与 260px 左侧抽屉。菜单始终通过未保存与保存中保护。内容独立滚动，编辑检查器按现有机制显示。
 
-Phase47 is the current local creative-workflow candidate (2026-10-26), with a production-dossier direction, four global entries and five contextual project stages. Official public GhostFibers, DriftWall, SideRays and FlowingMenu provide bounded home, directory, IP-showcase and project-overview effects. The home SVG material described in earlier phases is historical and no longer mounted there. Shared tokens, the Phase43 relationship board and quiet editors remain in place. The independent final reviewer returned PASS for the local candidate, with four original defects resolved and three evidence gaps closed; final-source TypeScript, full build and 140/140 core checks passed. This is an implemented local candidate, not owner approval, production acceptance or a whole-site React migration.
+看板以真实最近项目为大幅主视觉和纵向章节列表，项目目录为手动横滚卡片，同时保留完整搜索、筛选、排序、分页。项目没有默认封面字段；只有精确属于该项目的可访问素材引用可以装饰主视觉，并标明项目参考，缺图使用黑色排版。不得把素材、演员快照或示例项目伪作正式封面。
 
-**Key Characteristics:**
+项目主入口为故事、剧集、分镜、提示词，调用既有故事结构、文稿与审核接口。角色场景、小说、审阅、任务、制作及交付保留在更多工具中。提示词使用现有 prompt_note 文稿类型，没有另建一套假保存。
 
-- Shared semantic graphite, cream and copper paint across surfaces and controls.
-- Expressive bounded home, project-directory and IP showcases with stable, minimal editors.
-- Fixed serif headings and practical sans-serif user records.
-- Task-first disclosure, exact sources/versions and separate human review.
-- Stable-ID project/IP records across gallery and grid.
-- Compact relationship cards with selection-led, exact-ID evidence and a mobile list.
-- Four global destinations with one five-stage project context band.
-- Real request states, reduced motion, visible focus and guarded drafts.
+演员为大屏肖像展示，原图 contain，不裁切主体。同一图像提供 blur(26px) brightness(.28) saturate(.72) 的背景与原有边缘融合。性格、档案、经历全部在图像下方常驻，档案/衣橱/作品三项；旧 references 链接归入衣橱，身份链接仍可访问。
 
-## Colors
+衣橱以真实合集、造型和已绑定素材为数据源；提供当前合集搜索、槽位筛选、网格/列表、选中详情、编辑、新建、复制、排序与历史草稿。卡片标注绑定素材参考。列表摘要需要分批读取精确 spec 并校验 revision，未读完明确显示状态。选择卡片不表示全局已穿戴，不宣称 3D 或生成换装。作品场次仍通过既有 appearance 引用绑定精确版本。
 
-The frontmatter records canonical values from components/ui/studio-tokens.css. Roles apply across React roots, portals and native compatibility adapters.
+素材页保留完整 FRAME 功能。React 页面提供完整素材管理入口；原生页面使用紧凑工具栏、图像网格、选中后批量操作和宽幅图像详情。原图 contain/filter:none；可靠 modal 预览、原图下载、分类、组图、文稿、回收站、撤销和写入恢复全部保留。永久删除继续禁用。
 
-### Primary
+## 动效、可达性与真实状态
 
-- **Projection Copper** (primary, primary-hover) marks deliberate action; **Action Ink** keeps its text dark.
-- **Copper Focus** (ring) supplies the shared keyboard outline.
-- **Destructive Red** supplies explicit action styling; it grants no deletion or promotion authority.
+保留 React Bits GhostFibers、SideRays、AnimatedContent 及既有 GSAP/Embla 能力。仅装饰层动效，手动切换、不自动轮播。支持暂停、离屏停止、减少动态、低性能与无 WebGL 回退，内容默认可见。字段、错误、恢复、确认与无障碍名称不因精简而移除；触控动作最小 44px，键盘焦点明确，滚动条、选区与插入符跟随主题。
 
-### Secondary
-
-- **Success**, **Warning**, **Danger** and **Information** foreground/surface pairs supplement visible status words.
-- **Source Blue** and **Event Ochre** (graph-reference, graph-event and their surfaces) distinguish labelled relationships rather than introducing alternate action palettes.
-- **Project Sage**, **Project Clay**, **Project Slate** and **Graphic Ink** belong to illustration fields, not inferred covers, story meaning or review state.
-- **Print Paper/Ink** belongs to the scoped reference-print material.
-
-### Neutral
-
-- **Projection Graphite**, **Card Graphite** and **Popover Graphite** separate page, content and overlay layers.
-- **Warm Cream** and **Quiet Copy** form the reading hierarchy.
-- **Secondary Graphite**, **Muted Graphite** and **Active Graphite** serve secondary actions, tracks and selection.
-- **Boundary Graphite** marks structure; **Field Boundary** gives controls a stronger edge.
-
-**The Palette Authority Rule.** Shared controls and compatibility aliases resolve to the canonical semantic tokens; layout styles do not establish a second work-surface palette.
-
-Decorative WebGL light, real-title project SVG materials, historical metallic SVG stops, native OS option/file-picker dialogs and third-party React Flow controls/attribution are explicit presentation exceptions. They do not supply ordinary UI paint or imply verified project artwork.
-
-## Typography
-
-**Display Font:** CineWeave Display, the self-hosted Cormorant Garamond wordmark subset, with Georgia/serif fallback.
-
-**Heading Font:** CineWeave Heading, the self-hosted Noto Serif SC fixed-heading subset, with Noto Serif SC/serif fallback.
-
-**Body Font:** PingFang SC, Microsoft YaHei UI, system-ui, sans-serif. Technical JSON/identifiers and elapsed time use existing utility monospace.
-
-Fixed interface headings carry the serif voice; user-authored names and records keep the UI face. WOFF2 subsets and license notices live in public/fonts, without a remote font service. Changed fixed-heading characters require regenerated subsets or fallback.
-
-### Hierarchy
-
-- **Display:** compact wordmark; 23px on small screens. The intro separately uses a 60-130px clamp.
-- **Home headline:** the frontmatter UI-face clamp and leading for the actual selected project's title; 36px at up to 767px, with long-title wrapping.
-- **Headline:** fixed route headings, with observed 27px intermediate and 24px small-screen sizes.
-- **Title:** record/form headings; inspector identity uses 21px. Project illustration titles use a utility-face 22-38px clamp, then 27px on phones.
-- **Body / Control:** 14px working copy and shared controls. Fields become 16px at up to 767px.
-- **Prose:** preserved line breaks, long-word wrapping and a general-inspector maximum of 72ch.
-- **Label:** compact supporting text and badges. Smaller inherited metadata is not a reusable reading-size standard.
-- **Graph name / identity / label:** 16px/24px semibold names, 12px/18px supporting card identities, and 13px/20px lane headings and evidence chips. Supporting graph labels, counts, footnotes and mobile identity metadata intentionally use 12-13px; full reading and editing stay in the inspector. This scoped role does not normalize unrelated inherited tiny text.
-
-**The Record Voice Rule.** Fixed serif headings identify the interface; user records remain in the UI sans-serif face.
-
-## Layout
-
-Desktop uses a 72px top bar, 232px rail and flexible main column; the general inspector adds 350px. At up to 1250px, rail/inspector become 212px/310px. At up to 1050px, navigation and general detail use sheets. The compact top bar is 62px at up to 600px. Main horizontal padding is 32px desktop and 16px small-screen, with larger wide-layout insets.
-
-Working rhythm is 8px field, 16px group and 24px panel spacing, with 20px mobile panels. The first viewport prioritizes title, task action and necessary state. Advanced options, raw IDs, JSON and protocols open on demand; exact sources, versions, conflicts and review gates remain visible at decisions. Novel/screenplay creation stays with its page. Phase47 small-screen work headings align title and refresh actions in one row and hide the duplicated breadcrumb. The earlier Phase42 heading-action fit record remains historical.
-
-The fixed rail contains home, projects, actor IP and materials. Connection/authorization sits in its footer; native advanced tools open under secondary disclosure. Project pages place the picker and five stage tabs in one bordered context band, with an 18px gap and 24px following space. The band wraps and the tab strip scrolls as needed; global IP/material pages omit this project context. This changes navigation hierarchy while preserving existing routes, stable IDs and editing guards.
-
-Home uses a two-column opening and bounded reference print, then a real-project gallery. At up to 767px it becomes one column with 24px opening insets and a 245px maximum print. The same stable record nodes persist across gallery/grid. Native overflow before enhancement is a visual fallback, not a fully functional no-JavaScript application.
-
-The project directory keeps search/type controls above a bounded 460px DriftWall and a persistent index. Grid records use at least 210px columns on desktop and two columns with 12px gaps on small screens; list mode exposes descriptions. Static wall cards show the real title/type rather than photographs. The selected project's four-action FlowingMenu overview is bounded to 330px and becomes ordinary stage buttons on constrained clients. The five contextual tabs remain the complete project-stage navigation. The global IP library has a separate 190px-minimum SideRays header; the profile/wardrobe editor and create form stay quiet.
-
-The Phase43 desktop relationship board uses a 620px canvas with a 420px minimum. Its 224px by 88px cards pair across a project-role group, followed by a separate story-event lane; ordering comes from story_order then stable ID, without inventing affiliation or chronology. Open corridors carry routed relationships and evidence chips. Initial, resize and manual full-view fitting includes groups, cards, routes and labels; selection focus fits direct evidence. At up to 1050px, a person/event selector and direct-relationship list replace the canvas. Desktop also offers the list view. The existing scene strip remains story planning. The material inspector separately uses a 350px desktop column and sheet up to 440px; the general detail sheet is up to 400px. Sheet bodies scroll within the viewport and retain safe-area padding.
-
-## Elevation & Depth
-
-Working surfaces use tonal layering and fine borders; ordinary cards and controls remain flat. Shared popovers, dialogs and sheets use the canonical --cw-panel-shadow (0 4px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.16)); Phase43 cast cards reuse that token as a scoped graph layer. Focus uses an outline.
-
-Phase47 home uses one bounded GhostFibers background behind the work title/reference. SideRays is isolated to the global IP showcase; DriftWall and FlowingMenu have their own bounded directory areas. Static line material remains underneath the atmospheric canvases. Context/caption panels retain local 5px backdrop blur; the real reference remains unfiltered. Reduced transparency removes those panel blurs. The previous liquid-metal SVG remains historical source, not a second active home layer.
-
-**The Bounded Light Rule.** Keep ambient effects inside their home, directory or IP-showcase boundaries; keep reading text steady and editing surfaces stable. Use one atmospheric background per showcase.
-
-## Shapes
-
-Common controls use softly squared 6px corners; cards, tracks and overlays use 8px; compact badges and checkboxes use 4px. Fine one-pixel borders define rest states. The Button record variant removes ordinary padding, minimum height and border so specialized layouts own their geometry.
-
-Project fields, reference prints, portrait crops, scene cards and graph lanes keep content-specific shapes. The graph's 48px avatars/event icons and 6px round candidate/review dot are semantic content geometry; the dot's accessible wording and inspector preserve review meaning. Display crops do not change original media. Earlier home pill/circle geometry is not a global task-control standard.
-
-## Components
-
-### Shared control inventory
-
-The React workspace uses incumbent shadcn/Radix Button, Input/Textarea, NativeSelect, Checkbox, Tabs/ToggleGroup, DropdownMenu, Tooltip, Card/Badge, Dialog/AlertDialog and Sheet. studio-controls.css owns shared presentation; workspace styles own layout. Record-card layouts remain specialized.
-
-Advanced /studio, /materials and /sound preserve native media/document handlers while sharing tokens/control slots. This is compatibility coverage, not React/Radix migration. Radix hidden form inputs, native OS option/file-picker dialogs and React Flow controls/attribution remain exceptions.
-
-### Buttons
-
-Primary actions use copper and Action Ink. Outline uses Card Graphite and the field boundary; secondary uses Secondary Graphite; ghost/navigation is transparent until hover or selection. Shared nonprimary hover uses Active Graphite; primary uses its hover token. Selected/pressed actions retain explicit state and a copper boundary.
-
-Shared labels are 14px medium with 8px by 14px padding. Desktop normal/small minimum heights are 40px/36px; mobile at up to 767px uses 44px/40px. Icons use the normal square target. Disabled controls use .5 opacity and not-allowed; busy uses progress. Focus is a 2px ring outline with 3px offset. Color/border transitions last 160ms and stop for reduced motion. Scoped home controls retain source-specific focus offset and disabled opacity.
-
-### Inputs / Fields
-
-Input, Textarea and NativeSelect use Card Graphite, cream text, the stronger field border, 6px corners and 9px by 12px padding. Type is 14px desktop/16px mobile. Textareas start at 96px and resize vertically. Hover strengthens the edge; invalid uses Danger; disabled uses .5 opacity. Search has a visible label or accessible name. Native selection retains OS behavior.
-
-Checkboxes are 18px square with 4px corners and copper checked state; their label supplies a larger control-height target. Native radio/range compatibility controls share copper accent.
-
-### Tabs / ToggleGroup / Navigation
-
-Tabs/filter groups use a muted bordered track with 4px padding/gap and 6px choices. Inactive text is Quiet Copy; selected choices use Card Graphite, cream and the field boundary without shadow. Choices use 14px type and 36px/40px desktop/mobile minimums. Draft guards remain on editing-context changes.
-
-Floating tabs retain one moving indicator and immediate reduced-motion state; the shared controls determine current squared shape/paint. Mobile navigation opens a named sheet with explicit current state.
-
-Phase47 uses four persistent global choices and one contextual five-stage strip: story/characters, novel chapters, screenplay scenes, review and collaboration tasks. Current project stages also mark Projects as the current global destination. Connection/authorization retains the project picker without the stage strip. Existing URL state, Back/Forward and busy/unsaved-change guards apply to project, stage and native-tool navigation.
-
-### Project directory / Showcase effects
-
-GhostFibers, DriftWall, SideRays and FlowingMenu are actual public registry source, lazy-loaded into the existing React surface. Their registry/source hashes live in components/react-bits/sources.json; adaptations and license scope live in ADAPTATIONS.md and vendor/react-bits-LICENSE.md. The source is MIT + Commons Clause. FlowingMenu uses the installed Lucide arrow; no new dependency or Pro block/template was introduced.
-
-Directory search, type filter and wall/list controls retain a persistent project index. Session storage remembers only directory presentation preferences. Title-only SVG cards derive from actual project titles/types; no invented project image, unrelated catalog portrait or external default photograph supplies a cover. Ordinary keyboard/touch actions use the existing guarded project navigation; repeated wall copies stay outside keyboard order. The home catalog reference remains explicitly a reference, with no inferred casting or project-cover meaning.
-
-Atmospheric canvases are decorative and do not own content/actions. Home/IP expose pause controls; the directory exposes pause and list controls. Reduced motion, widths up to 767px, save-data or reported low cores/memory select static materials and ordinary buttons. Hidden/offscreen atmospheric effects stop and unavailable/lost WebGL retains the static background; local no-WebGL fallback was checked. Canvas density is capped at device-pixel ratio 1, and pointer-follow/click effects are disabled in these wrappers. FlowingMenu cleanup resets the cancelled animation-frame handle and timestamp so StrictMode effect replay permits real hover motion to restart.
-
-### Cards / Badges
-
-Cards use Card Graphite, semantic border, 8px corners and no resting shadow. Forms follow panel spacing. Badges use muted surface, visible words, border and 4px corners. State words and exact versions remain meaningful without color.
-
-Material tiles retain portrait crops, original-file access, selection and two-line 14px titles. Only an exact leading classification-code display prefix is removed; code appears once below. Stored names, IDs and inspector content remain unchanged. Catalog imagery is reference, never inferred casting or covers. Fixture content is not a design requirement.
-
-### Overlays / Menus / Tooltips
-
-Dialog, AlertDialog, Sheet, DropdownMenu and Tooltip share Popover Graphite, cream, semantic border, 8px corners and panel shadow. Descriptions use Quiet Copy at 14px/1.65. Menu items use small targets/highlight; tooltips use 12px/1.5 with a 260px maximum.
-
-Unsaved edits require confirmation before leaving. Closing a detail sheet returns focus to the trigger or canvas fallback. Confirmations preserve exact candidate/version consequences and separate human promotion. The native NEW COLLECTION admission guard is separate from independent catalog loading; one empty selected category does not establish unknown catalog state.
-
-### Relationship canvas / Inspector
-
-Phase43 rebuilds the graph body around compact cards: 48px avatar or event icon, 16px name and concise identity. Identity comes from the record's identity/role fields, with an event time label or truthful kind fallback. Portraits require a verified per-item MediaMap accepted by safeMedia; production currently supplies none, so name-derived initials remain visible. Fixture pictures are local test imagery and confer no casting relationship.
-
