+# MOMENTUM Studio production integration
+
+The user approved the local design and requested implementation, then added an actor wardrobe inspired by character costume selection systems. This stage integrates the confirmed visual system into the existing private Studio, using real projects, actors, looks and FRAME media references. No local seed projects, snapshot identities or in-memory save adapters are production data.
+
+Baseline: Site v102, source b543b145fa95d683f827a45854da596967d2a8f3. The existing Site ID, URL, private owner audience, D1/R2 bindings and MCP capability are retained. Latest source was fetched and fast-forwarded before editing; the local design candidate remains ignored and separate.
+
+Implementation scope: near-black/warm-white semantic theme and self-hosted fonts; left desktop navigation; project dashboard and scrolling project directory; story/episode/shot/prompt entry points backed by existing modules; large actor artwork with same-image blur and permanent biography; wardrobe backed by versioned actor-look APIs; full legacy FRAME asset management with a consistent compact image-first interface.
+
+Preserve: native owner access, all-owned-project policy, immutable revisions, CAS/idempotency, save/readback and unknown-result recovery, protected references, source media, human/P0 adoption boundaries, dirty/busy navigation guards, reduced-motion fallbacks, keyboard and mobile behavior. Do not add timelines, virtual try-on claims, permanent deletion, model generation tasks or new authorization prompts.
+
+Validation plan: scoped workflow/actor/material unit tests; TypeScript; full Studio Core stage review and source-readiness checks; complete Worker build and built-Worker smoke; desktop/mobile browser verification of real read paths and isolated authorized write/readback; independent review; source-helper commit/push/package; official private Site deployment and online version/access/MCP/readback verification. Record unavailable checks explicitly, and do not mark deployment complete from a build alone.
+
+## Verification — 2026-11-09
+
+- Site tests: 847/847 passed with `node --experimental-sqlite --experimental-strip-types --test tests/*.test.mjs`.
+- Core gate: 161/161 passed (`PYTHONUTF8=1 npm run review` on Windows); report inspected. The first attempt exposed default GBK decoding in a legacy migration test; UTF-8 mode fixed the execution environment.
+- TypeScript and full Worker build passed against the final implementation.
+- Built Worker: root redirect, React workspace, full native materials, sound, static modules, lookbook API, health/projects, D1 migration/backup/restore, anonymous and foreign-owner isolation passed. Used the already installed Codex Node 24.22.1 because default Node 22.15 lacks sqlite.backup. Existing lookbook additive checks now run at migration 0010, before later approved migrations intentionally evolve independent schemas; no migration bytes or production DB were changed.
+- Independent code review found and fixed a history-draft editor visibility defect and a late look-read/dirty-state race. Tab changes abort/invalidate wardrobe reads; historical drafts open the editable form.
+- Shared theme and native material checks passed (37/37). Existing metadata/download/trash/CAS/recovery tests remain enabled. No production write, generation task or media migration was used to exercise UI.
+- Local labelled fixture used the real HTTP/service handlers for actor identity, lookbook and saved looks. Its DB and media remain excluded from source/deployment. The preview resolver now prioritizes TSX to avoid colliding helper .mjs names, and reads the current labelled fixture project from its local receipt.
+- Browser verification is incomplete: CUA disconnected with transport closed before response, including a fresh independent read-only retry. No final desktop/mobile screenshots or real-owner browser write/readback can be claimed. Static/code/Worker checks are not visual acceptance.
+- Before publication, official Sites metadata confirmed live v102, owner role, custom access with one account recipient, no external viewers/groups/editors, and existing MCP plugin identity. Authenticated plugin capability read confirmed all_owned_projects/default_enabled; asset search succeeded. A Site-bypass read alone does not establish SIWC user context: Studio APIs correctly returned 401 and /workspace redirected to sign-in. No identity headers were forged to work around this boundary.
+
+## Wardrobe reference boundaries
+
+Official Naraka notices informed a unified wardrobe entry, actor-scoped selection, explicit outfit slots and collection grouping. The layout is this project's design inference; no client screenshots, game assets, 3D runtime or virtual try-on are reproduced.
+
+- [Closet entry from collection](https://www.narakathegame.com/news/update/20221013/35280_1046767.html)
+- [Hero-scoped preview improvements](https://www.narakathegame.com/news/update/20231101/33459_1117961.html)
+- [Shoes switch during outfit preview](https://www.narakathegame.com/news/update/20240709/33459_1166115.html)
+- [Wardrobe collection grouping](https://www.narakathegame.com/news/update/20260717/33459_1308163.html)
+
+The existing Site owns both website and plugin. Publication updates the same App/plugin; no duplicate plugin or changed scopes are needed. Deployment receipt and exact online static hashes are recorded separately after publication.
+
+
+## Browser recovery and preview repair
+
+After the browser transport recovered, the real React components were inspected at desktop 1280px and mobile 390px using the labelled persisted local fixture and existing HTTP handlers. Wardrobe cards/selection/detail, search no-match, slot filtering, edit/save/readback and the unsaved navigation confirmation passed. The mobile DOM had width 375px after the scrollbar and body width 375px (no horizontal overflow); navigation switched to the compact header/drawer. Portrait uses the original image with same-image blur; codex text remains below. Prompt, episode and storyboard routes rendered their existing real editors/structures. Screenshot evidence is local and excluded from deployment.
+
+Native FRAME inspection found a pre-existing mismatch: preview runtime still reset and rendered preview-technical after the underlying FRAME template and renderer had removed it. Removed these retired references and added composed-template reset-target checks. The native preview then opened the original image, showed existing metadata/classification/download actions and closed back to its asset trigger. No new browser error occurred after the repair. The local fixture's external ingest-protection status and account dashboard owner policy are unavailable by design; this is not evidence of live account authentication or ingestion.
+
+Site v103 (d25b1d276516b0f5c583dcc0112bf8f70c5124c6) deployed successfully. Its actor script and actor/workspace styles returned HTTP 200 and matched exact local SHA256; MCP stayed enabled and the same existing plugin read all 103 owned projects/default_enabled plus the real asset catalog. The preview repair is included in the next publication. The real-owner browser session now requires sign-in and stopped at the authentication service's security check; no CAPTCHA, credential or identity headers were bypassed. Live signed-in browser write/readback remains unverified.
